Z||000000||fierochild||09-15-2001||04:06 PM||||My 86GT with stock 2.8 will no longer hit hte rev limiter. At wot she will run up to 5000 in first but no further.  In second she tops out about 4800, and about 4500 in third.  Power seems to be normal through the lower revs.  Just kind of dies out.  I've been autocrossing this summer, and bumped the rev limiter several times.  Never had this condition before.  This has happened since having the cradle out for a clutch.  W hat have I screwed up? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||09-15-2001||05:42 PM||||maybe u just need to adjust the throttle cable, might not be opening all the way up. Worse case is the engines got a little too much wear now. I know mines not nearly as fast as it was 3 years ago.||||reg||1
